# Design Source of Truth

The supplied mockups define the intended visual result.

The specification files define the technical implementation.

## Workflow

Never immediately build a page from a mockup.

First analyse the supplied mockups.

Then create or update:

- specifications/design-system.md
- specifications/components.md
- specifications/pages/<page>.md

Only after the design specification exists may implementation begin.

## Mockup analysis

Analyse:

- page sections
- content hierarchy
- colors
- typography
- spacing
- container widths
- alignment
- image ratios
- border radii
- shadows
- button styles
- responsive behavior
- reusable components
- Elementor widget candidates

Do not invent invisible behavior from a static screenshot.

If something cannot reasonably be determined from the mockup, document the assumption.

## Responsive mockups

When desktop, tablet and mobile mockups are supplied, consider all of them before implementation.

Do not simply scale the desktop design down.

Identify:
- stacking changes
- hidden elements
- navigation changes
- image changes
- spacing changes
- typography changes
- reordered content

## Conflict resolution

Approved design-system specifications take precedence for implementation details.

Mockups remain the visual reference for final QA.

Do not silently alter the intended design because another layout would be easier to implement.